      "text": "We start with the expression \\(\\log_3 (27\\sqrt{3})\\). To evaluate this logarithm, we need to express the argument \\(27\\sqrt{3}\\) as a power of 3. We can rewrite \\(27\\sqrt{3}\\) as follows:\n\n\\[27 = 3^3\\]\n\\[\\sqrt{3} = 3^{1/2}\\]\n\nTherefore, we can write:\n\n\\[27\\sqrt{3} = 3^3 \\cdot 3^{1/2} = 3^{3 + 1/2} = 3^{7/2}\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\(\\log_3 (3^{7/2})\\). By the properties of logarithms, specifically the property \\(\\log_b (b^x) = x\\), we have:\n\n\\[\\log_3 (3^{7/2}) = \\frac{7}{2}\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\log_3 (27\\sqrt{3})\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7}{2}}\\).",
